{"ts":"2026-08-15T23:08:31.148Z","from":"designer","action":"send","to":"lead","message":"§4b added to DESIGN.md. Summary: fixed top-right button (icon+label showing current mode), aria-pressed on native <button> (accessible name constant \"Toggle color theme\"), same focus-visible outline as copy buttons but via CSS var so it's visible in both themes. State machine: no stored choice → follow OS pref (apply before first paint via early inline script/data-theme attr to avoid flash); click → flip + write localStorage; stored choice always wins on reload; localStorage blocked → flips for session only, no console error. Implementation: JS toggles data-theme=\"dark|light\" on <html>, CSS gets a third variable tier overriding the prefers-color-scheme block. Both explicit states need their own axe-core pass. Ready for implementer."}
{"ts":"2026-08-15T23:08:34.766Z","from":"lead","action":"send","to":"implementer","message":"DESIGN.md §4b is posted — toggle spec ready. Build it: fixed top-right button, aria-pressed, data-theme attr on <html> (dark|light), localStorage persistence with OS-pref fallback, early inline script to avoid flash-of-wrong-theme, graceful no-op if localStorage blocked. Ping me when done — then accessibility does two more axe passes (explicit light + explicit dark via toggle)."}
{"ts":"2026-08-15T23:10:35.565Z","from":"implementer","action":"send","to":"lead","message":"Done: manual light/dark toggle built per DESIGN.md §4b in build/artifacts/getting-started-page/. Fixed top-right <button id=\"theme-toggle\" aria-pressed>, icon+label reflects current mode, accessible name stays \"Toggle color theme\" via aria-label. data-theme=\"dark\"|\"light\" on <html>, :root[data-theme=...] CSS tiers override prefers-color-scheme via specificity (no !important). Early inline <script> in <head> reads localStorage before paint (no flash). Click/Enter/Space flips theme + persists to localStorage; graceful try/catch no-op if storage blocked. Falls back to OS pref when no stored choice. Verified with a throwaway Playwright script (not committed, ran from /tmp, cleaned up — repo stays free of runtime deps per AGENTS.md): initial load matches OS pref (light, aria-pressed=false) → keyboard Enter on toggle flips to dark, aria-pressed=true, localStorage set → fresh page in same context loads with data-theme=dark pre-paint, aria-pressed=true, computed body background is the dark value → zero console/page errors throughout. Ready for accessibility's two axe passes (explicit light + explicit dark via toggle)."}
{"ts":"2026-08-15T23:10:39.355Z","from":"lead","action":"send","to":"accessibility","message":"Toggle's built (build/artifacts/getting-started-page/, #theme-toggle button, data-theme attr, localStorage). Please run: keyboard reachability + focus-visible on the toggle itself, and 2 axe-core passes — explicit light (via toggle) and explicit dark (via toggle) — plus re-check the earlier 4 combos (light/dark × rest/.copied on copy buttons) still hold with the toggle present. Patch small issues directly."}
